nodecode-memtomem is a rewrite of memtomem's memtomem/memtomem:

  https://github.com/memtomem/memtomem
  commit b440f108ad42e349a1518c0dcf67bb23f0240936
  Apache-2.0, Copyright 2025-2026 DAPADA Inc. and memtomem contributors (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is packages/memtomem-hermes-plugin of that commit. Its
plugin.json, mcp.json and six skill files describe one local memory store that
several coding agents share; the six skills' five verbs keep their names and
their parameters (mem_search, mem_recall, mem_add, mem_index, mem_status), and
so does the shape of the data they reach: a store at ~/.memtomem, notes under
its memories/ directory, one markdown file per day, one "## " section per
entry, a "> created:" and "> tags:" blockquote header under each heading.
What this cell writes is the block the original's tools/memory_writer.py writes,
so a store it appends to keeps being read, by this cell and by the other
agents that share it, and what they write is read here. Search is BM25 over
the note sections, the original's default ranker, and the workflows the six
skills spell out are carried in the tools' descriptions and in (help :memtomem).

The original runs a Python MCP server (uvx --from memtomem[onnx]==0.7.4) that
indexes the notes into SQLite. What was rewritten is that server's five tools
as Lisp over the notes themselves; what was left out, and why:

  * The SQLite index, the embedding and reranker models, and every other
    provider the server can be configured with. A cell bundles no Python, so
    the store is read directly, with the ranker the original uses when no
    embeddings are configured (BM25); dense retrieval is not carried.
  * The rest of the server's tool surface: mem_do's context-gateway actions,
    ingest, export and import, the project tiers, and the file watcher that
    re-indexes changed files while the server runs. Nothing needs indexing here
    (a search reads the notes it needs), and the six skills call none of those
    actions.
  * The redaction guard the original applies to an added entry before it is
    written, and the idempotency key and the consolidation of similar entries.
    mem_add here appends the block and names a similar entry when it finds one.
  * The Hermes runtime itself: uvx, the MCP transport and the plugin manifest
    are the harness's, not the data's.

LICENSE is memtomem's repository LICENSE, unchanged.
